{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1333769-updating-moon-gifts-from-lore-of-the-forsaken","id":1333769,"title":"Updating Moon Gifts from Lore of the Forsaken","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-02T18:19:51-07:00","id":1333769,"title":"Updating Moon Gifts from Lore of the Forsaken","content":"So... over the past few months me and a couple of friends have been working on updates for some of the Moon Gifts from Lore of the Forsaken to 2e... and well here we go! My general design philosophy was to look at the 1e gift has a whole, take one or two facets from it as inspiration of a theme for the 2e, and expanding the other facets using that theme. Like for the Judge's Moon I original kept the &quot;damage mirroring&quot; power from 1e, but when 2e Gift of Agony had a facet that did mirroring damage, I mulled it over and decided for a capstone Facet I'd go with the &quot;Divine Judgement from above&quot; in applying a Bane. After all, Uratha got their weakness to Silver from Luna, right? (ssshhh The Forsaken/Pure don't know that they had that weakness in Pangea.) And I balanced it around the Promethean abilities, and the teaser we've had for Dark Eras 2 with the Cleverquick that can Apply a Bane as their Kith blessing.<br /> <br /> I still don't have an idea what to call the Ithaeur's 3rd Facet for the Witch's Moon Gift, and would love suggestions!<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Judge\u2019s Moon Gift</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Elodoth are the Walker\u2019s Between, the judges, envoys and masterminds of the Forsaken, the Elodoth wielding the Judge\u2019s Moon embody the Elodoth\u2019s role has a judge amongst Forsaken.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Grasp The Prey\u2019s Mind (\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With a short interaction the Elodoth becomes able to see what drives others, learning their dreams and goals. Giving the Elodoth an edge over the target.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Essence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Manipulation + Empathy + Honor - Target\u2019s Composure + Primal Urge (the target can choose not to resist)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Roll Results</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The target learns the Elodoth\u2019s Aspirations, granting +3 on social rolls to manipulate the Elodoth</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Elodoth fails to gain an understanding of the target.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success: The Elodoth learns the targets Aspirations, granting the Elodoth a [Honor] bonus on rolls made to socially manipulate the target. The bonus can be traded one for one to improve the Elodoth\u2019s Impression rating for the target. </span></span>This bonus lasts for the Chapter.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Elodoth learns of any Aspirations the target has recently fulfilled or moved on from.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Pangs of Guilt (\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Elodoth wielding the Judge\u2019s Moon becomes capable of forcing the prey to correct their actions, with a few words, piercing glare or subtle growl the Elodth forces their prey to address the wrong in their life.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Gift can only be used on a target once per lunar cycle.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Essence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Presence + Investigation + Honor \u2014 target\u2019s Resolve + Primal Urge (the target may choose not to resist)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Roll Results</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Elodoth dredges up their own wrongdoings. The character inflicts the Guilty Condition on themselves.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The target may feel a faint twinge of conscience, but nothing more.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The target gains the Guilty Condition, which can be resolved normally or by confessing to the Elodoth even if they are not involved. If the Elodoth uses the Gift again during the confession the target does not resolve the Guilty Condition, but must resolve it in the manner the Elodoth determines.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Elodoth gets to determine the resolution to the Condition on the initial activation, not the second activation.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Beguiled Hunter (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For the duration of the Facet\u2019s effects, the Elodoth adds his Honor Renown to the following dice pools as long as he is taking actions to pursue the Siskur-Dah:</span></span><ul><li>Actions during an Investigation, Social Chase (CofD pg. 86) or Social Maneuvering.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Facet can only be activated when the Elodoth gains the Siskur-Dah Condition.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Eye for Truth (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not all disputes are open and shut, sometimes forces conspire to sway the Elodoth\u2019s judgment one way or another. Wielding the power of the Judge\u2019s Moon, Elodoth become very hard to sway through mind control or illusions.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Essence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Presence + Investigation + Honor</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By surveying an area or scrutinizing an individual the Elodoth becomes aware of any illusionary, or mind-altering powers the target may be under. Initiating a Clash of Will with the creator of the illusion or whoever altered the target's mind.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Roll Results</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Elodoth is convinced an ally has influenced their mind, gaining the Paranoid Condition.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Elodoth does not detect anything awry.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Elodoth becomes aware of any Conditions impacting the mind of their target (such as altered memories), or illusions placed on the area (such as a Vampire's ability to Obfuscate). They can then initiate a Clash of Wills against the entity using illusions or altering the target's mind. If the target suffers from the Amnesia Condition from mundane sources, the Storyteller rolls (10-targets Integrity) in the clash pool.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This power also penetrates naturally occurring illusions such as a Changelings Mask, or the illusions over a Promethean\u2019s disfigurements.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This does not pierce a Demon\u2019s Cover, but the Elodoth can detect something awry with the Demon and attempt to initiate a Clash of Wills. If the Elodoth loses, they feel the illusion breaking away and see a normal human if the Elodoth wins the clash the Demon risks losing cover and the Elodoth will see the Demon\u2019s Demonic Form superimposed on the cover.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Elodoth gains the Informed Condition in regards to the entity attempting to deceive them with Magic.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Curse of Talion (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In legend Banes are quite often the result from breaking a rule or agreement. From Iron\u2019s hatred of Fae for a bargain being broken to Luna\u2019s curse of Silver onto werewolves for killing Father Wolf to Vampires burning under the gaze of Helios for a slight lost to history. History is full of creatures being punished with a weakness, at the peak of their power Elodoth walking the path of the Judge\u2019s Moon are capable of inflicting Banes on their enemies.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This power can only be used on targets that have violated an agreement with the Elodoth\u2019s pack, crossed into their territory willingly or are the subject of a Siskur-Dah.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unfortunately for Elodoth, this power does not work on the Idigam. Any failures to use this power on an Idigam are automatically Dramatic Failures. Successes and Exceptional Successes are treated as ordinary Failures.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 3 Essence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Presence + Intimidation + Honor versus target\u2019s Resolve + Primal Urge (Target\u2019s with the Guilty Condition applies the penalty from the Condition to the roll)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 week or the duration of the Siskur-Dah, whichever comes first.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Roll Results</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Elodoth instead curses themselves with the chosen Bane, and their chosen target automatically knows the Bane</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> No effect</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Elodoth inflicts a Bane of their choice upon the target. The target becomes aware of the Bane, and do everything in their power to avoid it. It is traditional for the Bane to be some sort of metal, or object/force occurring in nature\u2026 but the Claws of the Uratha is a valid Bane.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The bane lasts for an additional [Successes] days beyond the normal end time.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Stalker\u2019s Moon</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not all hunts involve shadowing prey silently or striking rapidly unseen, sometimes the Hunt requires the pack to have a person on the inside someone to cut off the escape routes of the prey. On those hunts the Forsaken turn to the Irraka of the Stalker\u2019s Moon to go ahead of the pack and infiltrate the Prey\u2019s home, so that all escape may be cut off. Even if it means gaining the trust of the prey only to betray them later.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Stalker\u2019s Spoor (\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While anyone can disguise their identity, only the Irraka with the Stalker\u2019s Moon may disguise their entire Spoor. Changing their scent to resemble something or someone else's, or even duplicating the scent of a packmate to lay down false trails</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Spoor lasts for a single scene but can be reactivated before wearing off.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Essence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Manipulation + Survival + Cunning</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Extended to create a new Spoor (Successes 10; each roll represents 5 minutes crafting the Spoor.), Instant to use a previously crafted Spoor</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Roll Results</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Irraka thinks they successfully disguise their Spoor, only to draw attention to their Uratha nature, their breath smells of raw meat, their hair like wet dog, or other tells the Storyteller comes up with.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Gift fails to work.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Irraka successfully disguises their Spoor in a manner of their choosing, or makes process creating a new Spoor. A Spoor crafted as an Extended Action can be stored and recalled later as an Instant action.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Spoor may be as detailed as they choose, sick or healthy, male or female, sweaty, freshly showered, etc. The Irraka if they choose can even decide to lay down the scent of animals, their packmates, or if they know it\u2026 the Prey themselves.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Irraka gains the Untraceable Condition. Which may be ignored if the purpose of the scent is to create a false trail.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Living Camouflage (\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While an Irraka may be capable of infiltrating any organize, some organizations require special skill sets in order to do their duty, but while an Irraka can disguise themselves as a doctor they may not be able to perform open heart surgery. But an Irraka wielding Living Camouflage can draw upon the spiritual resonance of the location to perform well enough to fulfill their duty or even steal the knowledge from someone in the field.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Essence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Manipulation + Larceny + Cunning vs Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance (if stealing Skill dots)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant to draw on the resonance of the location, Contested to draw the knowledge from an individual.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scene</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Roll Results</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> All failures the Irraka make using the skill become Dramatic automatically.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Irraka does not gain any skill dots.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Irraka successfully channels the resonance of the area and gains Skill dots equal to successes rolled up to a maximum of their Cunning Renown. The dots gained can not go above the Uratha\u2019s Primal Urge cap.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stealing skill dots grants an amount of Skill dots equal to the dots the victim possesses, plus the Irraka gains access to any applicable Merits and specialties the character possesses. Stealing skill dots requires the Irraka to render the victim unconscious, and remain unconscious for the duration. Most Irraka using this Facet restrain the victim and place them in a secure location on site or nearby. The Irraka can maintain the connection for [Cunning] kilometers/miles.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Irraka may also choose to borrow a packmates skill dots if the packmate has relevant skills, or merits. Doing so prevents the packmate from rolling the skill, but it does not require the packmate to be unconcious.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> the Irraka also gains the Inspired Condition applied to the Skill in question.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Devious Hunter (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No matter how tight security is or how thoroughly you investigate their background, an Irraka of the Stalking Moon always manages to infiltrate a group.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Facet can only be activated when the Irraka gains the Siskur-Dah Condition.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Essence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The full duration of Siskur-Dah</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For the Duration of the SIskur-Dah, the Irraka adds her Cunning Renown to the following dice pools as long as they are on the hunt:</span></span><ul><li>Subterfuge rolls to deceive or trick the Prey.</li> <li>Larceny checks to create disguises, forge documents, conceal evidence, or hide objects on your person.</li> <li>Social rolls to infiltrate in pursuit of the Prey (such as Subterfuge to lie your way past guards, Persuasion to bribe a doorman, or Socialize to blend in at a party).</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Mercurial Hunter (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Danger of the Irraka not only lies in their ability to infiltrate a location with a fake identity, stealth, or a silver tongue. It\u2019s in their ability to be in unexpected places, at unexpected times.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While on the Siskur-Dah the Irraka\u2019s form becomes quite mercurial, able to take the form of inanimate objects with no moving or electrical parts. A chair, a statue, or a paperweight are all valid options. While disguised as an inanimate object the Irraka remains aware of their environment.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The full duration of Siskur-Dah</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Irraka gains a pool of points equal to their Cunning, that can be used in the following ways:</span></span><ul><li>Increase or decrease their size by 1 to become a copy of an object (minimum size 1)</li> <li>Add a die to a stealth roll as they blend into the background</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Disguising themselves has an object can be done reflexively by spending an Essence.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Lair\u2019s Brands (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mastery of the Stalker\u2019s Moon lets the Irraka disguise the very Renown marks seared into Flesh by Lunes, making them look more or less Renowned than they are\u2026 or even disguising their Renown Brands has the Scars adoring the Pure.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Irraka under this Gifts influence is incapable of raising Renown normally and must either cancel its effects or wait for them to wear off. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Essence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Manipulation + Subterfuge + Cunning</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Extended (1 Success required per dot of Renown raised or lowered, an additional five successes are required to disguise their Renown as that of the Pure\u2019s)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Roll Results</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Irraka\u2019s suppresses their Renown and losses the ability to flare their Renown.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Irraka fails to disguise their Renown.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Irraka successfully disguises their Renown. Attempting to flare Renown lets the Irraka choose between shedding their disguise, or having the disguised Renown marks show themselves. They do not gain Renown conditions unless shedding their disguise in which case they gain the Cunning Condition.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With extra work, the Renown marks of the Pure can be imitated. Letting the Irraka pretend to be a member of the Pure.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The effects of the disguise last for one lunar cycle unless dispelled by Flaring Renown.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Additional successes are their own reward</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Second Life (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes a successful hunt requires getting close to the prey, and no one is closer to a Uratha then their pack mates. An Irraka wielding this Facet may successfully pretend to join a pack, though getting to the point where they are offered membership is another story. The Irraka appears to have the Totem bonus for all intents and purposes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 2 Essence per Week</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Manipulation + Subterfuge + Cunning versus the Totem\u2019s Finesse + Resistance</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Contested</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Roll Results</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Irraka\u2019s Totem bond with its pack severs, making the Irraka\u2019s totem think that the Irraka has betrayed them. The Irraka must work to rejoin his pack, as well as sever his new Pack bond.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Irraka fails to infiltrate the rival, and the Totem becomes aware that something is suspicious about the Irraka.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Irraka successfully spoofs the pack bond, with the new packs totem none the wiser. The Irraka is unable to draw upon the benefits the infiltrated pack\u2019s totem provides, the infiltrated pack can still target them with Pack targeting abilities, but the Irraka has to reflexively spend a single point of Essence to let the powers affect them. The Irraka may also use their pack-targeting abilities on the infiltrated pack, which also costs an additional essence.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Irraka remains capable of drawing upon their normal pack benefits They are also able to use Target impacting Facets on their normal pack with no additional costs. (Such as using Pack Awareness to report in).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Irraka gains a [Cunning] bonus to faking the Totem provided bonus.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Irraka is capable of drawing upon the totem benefits from the infiltrated pack, but doing so requires the Irraka to spend a point of essence. The totem benefits last for the scene.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Witch\u2019s Moon Gift</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Shadow-Speaking (\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mortal channeling the dead to speak through them has been a part of human sorcery for untold millennia, Ithaeur practicing the Witch\u2019s Moon learn to channel spirits in order to learn what happened in an area without having to find a locus in order to cross over and speak with Spirits or to negotiate with spirits when it\u2019s impractical to cross over to the Gauntlet.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Essence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Wits + Occult + Wisdom</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Roll Results</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Uratha gains the Open Condition for spirits in the areas and may find Spirits attempting to use their Manifestations on them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Ithaeur fails to create a bridge between the Shadow and themselves.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Ithaeur successfully establishes a bridge between themselves and the Shadow. Any Spirits on the other side of the Gauntlet may reach across the bridge and communicate through the Ithaeur, the Spirit may only speak through the Ithaeur, and hear through their ears and can not control the Ithaeur. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The local spirits are impressed with the Ithaeur, moving their impression with the Ithaeur one level up on the impression chart for Social Maneuvering. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Projected Senses (\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the senses of the Uratha are powerful, they do have limits, they can not see through walls, into obstacles, scents need a trail to be followed, etc. An Ithaeur is capable of covering far more territory mentally projecting their senses and capable of covering ground at the speed of thought.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Essence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Wits + Occult + Wisdom</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Roll Results</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Uratha senses all disconnect, sight travels one way, while their hearing and sense of smell go in two different directions. The Ithaeur applies the Unaware Condition to themselves (except the penalty is the Ithaeur\u2019s own Wisdom score) as they struggle to control their senses.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Ithaeur fails to project their senses</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Ithaeur successfully projects their Wolf senses from their body, they can cover a lot more territory on the search for their Prey. Travelling at the speed of thought, the Ithaeur can project their senses through walls, the ground looking for cave systems or even into overhead planes. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While projected the Ithaeur is unaware of what is happening around their body, but can still feel is someone touches them or if they get injured.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This gift can only be used effectively on their own sanctified territory, beyond that it only lets the Ithaeur see a vague outline of landscape, specific features such as doors, trees, and people are impossible to determine. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Regions of the pack territory represented by Merits such as Safe Place or Den, grant the Ithaeur a perception bonus equal to the merit dot rating, and can be surveyed even if not within a sanctified territory. Only the highest rated merit can apply for a specific location (such as a Den containing a Safe Place or vice versa).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This power only lets the Ithaeur project their senses, and does not grant any abilities to pierce attempts at supernatural concealment or disguises. Nor can other sensory gifts be used while projected.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Ithaeur is able to project their senses while maintaining a perfect awareness of their body. Projecting their senses somewhere does require an Instant action to focus on the new location.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">____ Hunter (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Ithaeur on the hunt is a master of spiritual sorcery.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Facet can only be activated when the Ithaeur gains the Siskur-Dah Condition</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Essence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The full duration of Siskur-Dah</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For the duration of the Facet\u2019s effects, the Ithaeur adds her Wisdom Renown to the following dice pools as long as she is in the Shadow or taking actions to pursue the Siskur-Dah\u2019s prey.</span></span><ul><li>Any Influence rolls they have been granted from Rites, Talens, Lodge Sorcery or Fetishes.</li> <li>Any rites they perform as the Ritemaster.</li> <li>Adds their Wisdom to Occult rolls. (This does not stack with other bonuses, such as Lodge Sorcery.)</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Shadow Discord (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirits do not have to cross the Gauntlet to meddle in the flesh, many have powers that reach across the Gauntlet. Powerful Ithaeur wielding the Witch\u2019s Moon can if not prevent, at least make it difficult.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 2 Essence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Manipulation + Occult + Wisdom</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Day</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Roll Results</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Ithaeur\u2019s next attempt to reach is penalized by their own Wisdom.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Ithaeur fails to interfere with nearby spirit\u2019s ability to Reach.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> All spirits (on either side of the Gauntlet) within [Success * 100 meters/yards] find any rolls reaching across the Gauntlet, or involving Influence penalized by the Ithaeur\u2019s Wisdom.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This penalty does not apply to any Spirits in the pack, such as the Pack\u2019s Totem.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Additional successes are their own reward.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Spirit Cage (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not all spirits need or even deserve destruction, discorporation, or being hounded back into the Shadow, Ithaeur wielding the Witch\u2019s Moon can draw a spirit into their own body and cage it within, creating a prison of their own body.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Ithaeur wishing to imprison a spirit must first initiate a grapple, once the power is enable the spirit is unable to break free unless they use the Break Free maneuver [Ithaeur\u2019s Wisdom] times. Some spirits may choose to accept imprisonment to escape Shadow Politics or Essence Bleed while in the flesh until such a time as the Ithaeur can enter the Gauntlet and release them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Essence equal to the Rank of spirit to be imprisoned, additional essence can be spent to draw on the Spirit's power as described below.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Strength + Brawl + Wisdom vs the Spirit\u2019s Rank + Power (if resisting)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Extended (10 successes; each roll represents one turn of the grapple)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 lunar cycle, can be renewed for an additional [Spirit\u2019s Rank] Essence.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Roll Results</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Spirit breaks out of the grapple and becomes immune to further uses of this power for the rest of the Lunar cycle.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> No progress is made. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Progress is made, if the Spirit is successfully imprison the Ithaeur is able to tap into the Spirit's power.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tapping into the spirit\u2019s power requires the Ithaeur to spend a point of Essence and to roll an appropriate social attribute + social skill vs the Spirits Resistence. This roll depends on how exactly the spirit was imprisoned (forceful imprisonment requiring Presence + Intimidation for example). Once convinced the Ithaeur gains an amount of dread powers equals to the Spirits Numina, these Dread powers last for the scene and may have additional costs as per the individual Dread Power. The Dread Powers the Spirit provides should be agreed upon with the storyteller at the moment of imprisonment.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While imprisoned the Spirit is immune to Essence Bleed, and can in fact be sustained indefinitely for as long as the Ithaeur is willing to spend the Essence.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the Ithaeur dies while the spirit is imprisoned, the imprisoned spirit takes an amount of Aggravated damage equal to the Elodoth\u2019s Stamina, as well as loses all their Essence. The Spirit is then ejected from the Ithaeur\u2019s body.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Ithaeur does not have to roll to access the Dread Powers provided by the spirit.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":4737,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","user":"Afro Luigi","date":".  Judge's Moon first dot didn't have a duration, it does now. 09-02-2019, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T18:39:29-07:00","id":1333771,"title":"","content":"Oh! the reason I have two versions of the Stalker's Moon 3rd dot is that I was having trouble coming up with a 3rd dot that was different enough from the Core one, and came up with Mercurial Hunter before I fixed Devious Hunter to its present state. And am still sort of swinging back and forth on which one is better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T18:53:21-07:00","id":1333774,"title":"","content":"Wow! I haven't had time to read through all of it, but that is a tone of work you've done. Awesome job!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}